  "source_brief": "# Regolith Radiation Shielding over Habitat Module A\n\n**Site.** Habitat Module A is already in place on its foundation, 10 m long and 4 m in diameter, on firm ground 400 m north of the landing pad. A borrow area of loose regolith lies 80 m to the west. The depot is at the borrow area; no recharging.\n\n**Structures.**\n\n1. Shielding mound: cover the module with 1.5 m of regolith on the sides and 2 m on top, about 120 cubic metres of fill, placed in three compacted lifts from a borrow pit.\n2. Borrow pit: a 15 m by 10 m excavation 1 m deep that supplies the fill; its floor is graded afterwards so it can serve as a future storage pad.\n\n**Fleet.** EX1 (excavator, 5000 Wh), HL1, HL2 and HL3 (haulers, 3000 Wh each), CP1 (compactor, 3500 Wh) and SV1 (surveyor, 1500 Wh). Each battery is the budget for the whole job.\n\n**Deadline.** 9 days.\n\n**Operational constraints.**\n\n- Each lift is compacted before the next lift is placed; the surveyor checks the final thickness.\n- Haulers do not enter the mound zone while the compactor is working in it.\n- Only one robot may work inside a zone at a time.\n"
 },
